\section*{Questions in Geometric Group Theory — Q 2.16}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a mathematical result relevant to this question in the selected manuscript. A specific Artin group on 116 generators is claimed to have no proper cocompact isometric action on a proper CAT(0) space.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Result 1.} For an Artin matrix \(M\) on 116 generators with off-diagonal entries only in \(\{2,3,\infty\}\), the constructed Artin group \(A_M\) is claimed to have no action that is simultaneously isometric, proper, and cocompact on any nonempty proper CAT(0) metric space. In quantified form,
\[
 \nexists X,\ A_M\curvearrowright X:\quad
 X\text{ proper CAT}(0),\quad\text{action proper and cocompact}.
\]
The metric space is required to be proper, and the exclusion is independent of dimension.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Stable translation lengths and centralizer characters impose quantitative braid constraints. Six asymptotic sectors and labeled triangular diagrams yield a local winding count incompatible with those constraints; a finite Artin matrix realizes the contradictory configuration.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The main 116-generator example refutes the broader finite-rank/proper-target version. It is not a spherical-type counterexample, so the separately requested finite-type version remains unanswered. This entry records partial support; complete coverage of the question is not established by this catalogue.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 254, the scope includes finite-rank Salvetti contractibility, the 116-generator Artin CAT(0) counterexample, and arbitrary parabolic intersections with closure consequences. Each has its own Comparator statement. The listed Comparator files are \texttt{ArtinCAT0.lean}, \texttt{ArtinParabolicIntersections.lean}, \texttt{HarmonicArtin.lean}. Named declarations include \texttt{OAI.ArtinCAT0.main}, \texttt{OAI.HarmonicArtin.salvetti\_cover\_contractible}. This site has not executed the Lean code. The scope descriptions do not certify the remaining manuscript arguments.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these manuscripts to work by an internal model. Its release cautions that arguments without formalization can contain mistakes. This catalogue has not independently checked the proofs; the labels report the mathematical claims attributed to OpenAI.

